#: ../../02_decentralchain/07_oracle.rst:96
msgid "For each token it describes, it writes entries whose key ends in the token ID in angle brackets: ``status_<ASSET_ID>`` and ``version_<ASSET_ID>`` (integers), and ``ticker_``, ``link_``, ``email_``, ``logo_`` (a data URI) and ``description_<LANG>_`` strings. ``status`` is ``2`` verified, ``1`` detailed, ``0`` not verified, ``-1`` suspicious or ``-2`` scam. A verified or detailed token must have every field; the others need only the version and the status."
